WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.040
If you want to understand AI alchemy, start here.

00:02.040 --> 00:03.400
Do not begin with a giant stack.

00:03.400 --> 00:04.720
Begin with one useful behavior.

00:04.720 --> 00:07.400
First, pick the outcome—not the tool, the outcome.

00:07.400 --> 00:09.640
Maybe it is replying to leads faster,

00:09.640 --> 00:13.240
summarizing research, or turning a missed call into a booked appointment.

00:13.240 --> 00:19.360
Second, install one skill that handles that job clearly.

00:19.360 --> 00:24.360
Third, connect the skill to one trigger, one input, and one output.

00:24.360 --> 00:28.840
Fourth, run it in the real world and watch where it breaks.

00:28.840 --> 00:34.520
That is the whole game: not more software, better loops.

00:34.520 --> 00:38.960
One working skill becomes a workflow.

00:38.960 --> 00:41.040
One workflow becomes an operating system.

00:41.040 --> 00:45.320
That is how you move from automation as a demo to automation as leverage.
